        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152">

                <pb facs="0314" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg142"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 857.857/82</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Havre</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Osborne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Havre</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 23, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 4 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Skrim</hi>, unarmed, proceeding in
                    ballast from Tréport to Cardiff, was sunk by bombs by German submarine, after
                    warning, February 19, 20 miles from Tréport. Crew 14 including Porto Rican,
                    Louis Pinto, were in lifeboats about 20 hours. Depositions captain and Pinto
                    taken.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Osborne</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
